IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- THE CORE: the nouns every part of the encoding shares.  DECLARE only, no rules, no #EVAL.
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- THE MEMBERSHIP TEST for this file: could a witness of ordinary competence testify to the fact,
-- or does answering it require reading the Rules?  Only the first kind is here.  "The Court
-- may extend the time" is a rule and is in no core; "the date on which the claimant was served"
-- is a fact and is.
--
-- Money is a NUMBER of Singapore dollars.  A date is a DATE, written `Date day month year`.
-- A part never edits this file and never waits for it.  A type or constructor it needs and
-- this file lacks is defined in the part's own module under the part's own label prefix and
-- recorded in the part's NEEDS-CORE.md.
--
-- COLLISIONS CHECKED.  daydate defines `Monday` to `Sunday`, `January` to `December`, `May`,
-- `Day`, `Month`, `Year`, `Week` and `Date`, as numbers or functions.  No constructor below
-- uses one of them, and a part must not either: a constructor named like one of those is
-- ambiguous in every file that imports daydate.

-- ===========================================================================
-- Courts, and who acts in them.  (O 1 r 3(1): "Court", "Judge", "Registrar", "officer")
-- ===========================================================================

-- The places where proceedings under the Rules are heard.  The Family Division and the
-- Singapore International Commercial Court are here because O 1 r 2(9) and (10) name them.
DECLARE `Court level` IS ONE OF
    `General Division`
    `Appellate Division`
    `Court of Appeal`
    `District Court`
    `Magistrate's Court`
    `Singapore International Commercial Court`
    `Family Division`

-- Which establishment the court belongs to.  The Rules often say "Supreme Court or State Courts"
-- and the Fourth Schedule has a column for each.  A part takes this as a fact about the case.
DECLARE `Court system` IS ONE OF
    `Supreme Court`
    `State Courts`

-- Who takes a decision in a court.  `The court itself` is the court as a body, for example "the
-- General Division".  `A Judge` is a judge of the High Court (either Division) or of the Court
-- of Appeal.  A District Judge is separate because O 1 r 3(1) "Court" and "Judge" name one.
DECLARE `Decision maker` IS ONE OF
    `The court itself`
    `A Judge`
    `A District Judge`
    `A Magistrate`
    `The Registrar`

-- A decision-maker sitting in a court: the shape of the thing O 1 r 3(1) "Court" talks about.
DECLARE Sitting HAS
    `sitting court level` IS A `Court level`
    `sitting decision maker` IS A `Decision maker`

-- What a court gives: O 3 r 4(1) says "judgment, order or direction".
DECLARE `Kind of decision` IS ONE OF
    `A judgment`
    `An order`
    `A direction`

-- ===========================================================================
-- The people in an action.  (O 1 r 3(1): "claimant", "defendant", "third party", "non-party")
-- ===========================================================================

-- The part a person plays in an action or an appeal.  A person in the position of a claimant
-- in a counterclaim is a `Claimant` here: the role is the position, not the pleading.
DECLARE `Role in the action` IS ONE OF
    Claimant
    Defendant
    `Third party`
    `Fourth party`
    Appellant
    Respondent
    `Non-party`

-- What kind of person.  O 4 r 1 sorts persons by age and treats entities separately.
-- `Entity` is "any body of persons, whether incorporated or unincorporated" (O 1 r 3(1)).
DECLARE `Kind of person` IS ONE OF
    `Natural person` HAS `age in years` IS A NUMBER
    Entity           HAS `incorporated` IS A BOOLEAN

-- How the person is acting in the action: for themselves, or through someone.
DECLARE `How a party acts` IS ONE OF
    `Acts in person`
    `Acts by solicitor`
    `Acts by litigation representative`

-- One person in one action: the unit a seat layer fills in from what the person can state.
DECLARE Litigant HAS
    `litigant role`   IS A `Role in the action`
    `litigant kind`   IS A `Kind of person`
    `litigant acting` IS A `How a party acts`

-- ===========================================================================
-- The documents.  (O 1 r 3(1): "originating claim", "pleading", "summons", ...)
-- ===========================================================================

-- The documents O 1, O 3 and O 6 name.  A document the Rules name that is not here is a
-- STRING in the part that needs it, or a type under the part's own label prefix.
DECLARE `Document kind` IS ONE OF
    `Originating claim`
    `Originating application`
    `Statement of claim`
    `Defence`
    `Defence and counterclaim`
    `Reply`
    `Reply to a defence and counterclaim`
    Summons
    `Summons without notice`
    Affidavit
    `Notice of intention to contest or not contest`
    `Notice of appeal`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Time.  (O 3 r 3 "Calculation of time"; O 1 r 3(1) "non-court day", "working day")
-- ===========================================================================

-- The units the Rules count in: "14 days", "7 clear days", "7 working days", "5 weeks",
-- "3 months", "48 hours".  `Clear days` and `Working days` are O 3 r 3(5) and O 1 r 3(1).
DECLARE `Time unit` IS ONE OF
    Days
    `Clear days`
    `Working days`
    Weeks
    Months
    Hours

-- Whether the period runs forward from an event or back from it: "within 14 days after" or
-- "not less than 7 clear days before".
DECLARE `Count direction` IS ONE OF
    `After the anchor`
    `Before the anchor`

-- A period as a rule states it: how many, in what unit, counted which way.
-- A rule writes its period as a constant of this type, so the number stays where the text puts it.
DECLARE Period HAS
    `period length`    IS A NUMBER
    `period unit`      IS A `Time unit`
    `period direction` IS A `Count direction`

-- The public holidays that the person asking states fall in the range of dates concerned.
-- A "non-court day" is a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday (O 1 r 3(1)); the Rules do not say
-- which days are public holidays, so this is a fact the asker supplies.
DECLARE `Court calendar` HAS
    `public holidays` IS A LIST OF DATE

-- A date and a time of day.  The time of day is minutes after midnight, so that 5 p.m. is 1020
-- and "before 5 p.m." (O 7 r 8) is a plain comparison with no gap at exactly 5 p.m.
DECLARE Moment HAS
    `day of the moment`      IS A DATE
    `minutes after midnight` IS A NUMBER

-- ===========================================================================
-- Service and filing.  (O 6, O 7, O 8, O 28)
-- ===========================================================================

-- How a document reached the person: the headings of O 7, plus the electronic filing service of O 28.
DECLARE `Method of service` IS ONE OF
    `Personal service`
    `Ordinary service`
    `Substituted service`
    `Service through the electronic filing service`

-- Where the person served was: in Singapore or out of it.  The periods in O 6 differ by this.
DECLARE `Place of service` IS ONE OF
    `Served in Singapore`
    `Served out of Singapore`

-- One act of service, as a witness would state it.  Whether it counts as effected, and on what
-- day, is O 7 r 8 and O 28 r 10 and r 12: a rule, so not here.
DECLARE `Service event` HAS
    `service of`      IS A `Document kind`
    `service method`  IS A `Method of service`
    `service place`   IS A `Place of service`
    `service moment`  IS A Moment

-- One act of filing, as a witness would state it: the document and the moment the filing system
-- records.  The deemed time of filing is O 28 r 10, a rule, so not here.
DECLARE `Filing event` HAS
    `filing of`     IS A `Document kind`
    `filing moment` IS A Moment

-- ===========================================================================
-- The action.  (O 1 r 2 "Revocation, transitional provisions and application")
-- ===========================================================================

-- The facts about an action that O 1 r 2 asks before any other rule applies.
DECLARE Action HAS
    `action commenced by`  IS A `Document kind`
    `action commenced on`  IS A DATE
    `action court level`   IS A `Court level`
